{"imamate-of-futa-jallon":{"img":"/images/states/imamate-of-futa-jallon.jpg","cr":{"a":"HetmanTheResearcher","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Improved_Flag_of_the_Imamate_of_Futa_Djallon_(1896-1912).svg"}},"igala-kingdom":{"img":"/images/states/igala-kingdom.jpg","cr":{"a":"Commons en Rollebon Original uploader was Rollebon at nl.wikipedia","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Igala.jpeg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-salem":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-salem.jpg","cr":{"a":"","l":"CC BY-SA 2.0 de","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salem_Front_NO.jpg"}},"italian-libya":{"img":"/images/states/italian-libya.jpg","cr":{"a":"F l a n k e r","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1861-1946)_crowned.svg"}},"ijebu-kingdom":{"img":"/images/states/ijebu-kingdom.jpg","cr":{"a":"Source: Henry B. Lovejoy, “Re-Drawing Historical Maps of the Bight of Benin Hinterland, c. 1780.” Canadian Journal of...","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oyo_Empire_at_Its_Greatest_Extent,_c._1780_(5).jpg"}},"ifni":{"img":"/images/states/ifni.jpg","cr":{"a":"Army Map Service, Corps of Engineers","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ifni_txu-oclc-6949452-nh29-10.jpg"}},"isle-of-man":{"img":"/images/states/isle-of-man.jpg","cr":{"a":"Fry1989 eh?","l":"CC0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Isle_of_Mann.svg"}},"ilergetes":{"t":"The leading Iberian people of the Lleida plain, whose chiefs Indibilis and Mandonius switched between Carthage and Rome in the Second Punic War.","o":"The Ilergetes occupied the plains of the Segre and Cinca rivers around modern Lleida from the 5th century BCE, with their capital at Iltirta. By the late 3rd century BCE they were among the most powerful peoples of north-eastern Iberia.","r":"They were ruled by princes who could raise large armies and dominate neighbouring peoples. Their economy rested on the cereal plains of the Segre, and Iltirta minted coins with an Iberian legend. During the Second Punic War their leaders Indibilis and Mandonius first served Carthage, then joined Scipio in 209 BCE.","e":"In 206 and 205 BCE the brothers revolted against Rome; Indibilis died in battle and Mandonius was handed over and executed. The Ilergetes were absorbed into Hispania Citerior, and Iltirta became Roman Ilerda, where Caesar defeated Pompey\u0027s legates in 49 BCE.","ru":["Indibilis","Mandonius"],"re":"Iberian religion","la":"Iberian","c":"medium"},"italian-islands-of-the-aegean":{"img":"/images/states/italian-islands-of-the-aegean.jpg","cr":{"a":"F l a n k e r","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1861-1946)_crowned.svg"}},"inca-empire":{"img":"/images/states/inca-empire.jpg","cr":{"a":"Made and uploaded by Huhsunqu.","l":"CC BY-SA 2.5","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Inca_Empire.svg"}},"indo-greek-kingdom":{"img":"/images/states/indo-greek-kingdom.jpg","cr":{"a":"Classical Numismatic Group","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Hippostratos.jpg"}},"islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-2021-present":{"img":"/images/states/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-2021-present.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original: Taliban Vector: Lexicon","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Taliban.svg"}},"imagawa-clan-domain":{"img":"/images/states/imagawa-clan-domain.jpg","cr":{"a":"Mukai","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_crest_Imagawa_Akadori.svg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-weingarten":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-weingarten.jpg","cr":{"a":"","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Weingarten_Kloster_1500.jpg"}},"inner-austria":{"img":"/images/states/inner-austria.jpg","cr":{"a":"Joseph Carl Kindermann, gestochen von Christoph Junker","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AvI_Provinz_Inner%C3%B6sterreich.jpg"}},"indigetes":{"t":"The Iberian people of the Empordà, neighbours of Greek Emporion, whose hill town at Ullastret is the largest Iberian site in Catalonia.","o":"The Indigetes occupied the Empordà plain of north-east Catalonia from about the 6th century BCE. Their growth was closely linked with the founding of Emporion by Greeks around 575 BCE, and part of their community lived beside the Greek town, which Livy describes as a double city.","r":"Their largest settlement, at Ullastret, was a walled hill town with towers, temples and grain silos, showing strong Greek influence in its architecture and imports. The Indigetes exchanged grain and other goods for Greek pottery and wine, and minted coins with the Iberian legend Untikesken. Their political organisation was probably based on town elites.","e":"They took part in the north-eastern revolt against Rome and were subdued by Cato in 195 BCE. Ullastret was abandoned soon afterwards, and the Indigetes merged with the population of Roman Emporiae and Hispania Citerior.","re":"Iberian religion","la":"Iberian","c":"medium"},"iga-confederacy":{"img":"/images/states/iga-confederacy.jpg","cr":{"a":"Ash_Crow","l":"CC BY 2.5","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Iga.svg"}},"idel-ural-state":{"img":"/images/states/idel-ural-state.jpg","cr":{"a":"Himasaram","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Idel-Ural_State.svg"}},"italian-governorate-of-montenegro":{"img":"/images/states/italian-governorate-of-montenegro.jpg","cr":{"a":"F l a n k e r","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1861-1946)_crowned.svg"}},"iwellemmeden-kel-dinnik":{"img":"/images/states/iwellemmeden-kel-dinnik.jpg","cr":{"a":"Felix Dubois (author of book)","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Niqab_on_Tuareg.jpg"}},"imamate-of-oman":{"img":"/images/states/imamate-of-oman.jpg","cr":