IV.svg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-gandersheim":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-gandersheim.jpg","cr":{"a":"Misburg3014","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bad-Gandersheim-Stiftskirche-Seite-vorn.JPG"}},"ile-bourbon":{"img":"/images/states/ile-bourbon.jpg","cr":{"a":"Superbenjamin","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armoiries_R%C3%A9union.svg"}},"italian-east-africa":{"img":"/images/states/italian-east-africa.jpg","cr":{"a":"F l a n k e r","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1861-1946)_crowned.svg"}},"italian-social-republic":{"img":"/images/states/italian-social-republic.jpg","cr":{"a":"See below.","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy.svg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-essen":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-essen.jpg","cr":{"a":"Ralf Hüls","l":"CC BY-SA 2.0 de","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%BCnster_Essen_Kreuzgang_20060326.jpg"}},"iraca":{"img":"/images/states/iraca.jpg","cr":{"a":"Petruss","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Floresta_Boyaca_-_Panoramica.JPG"}},"imperial-british-east-africa-company":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-british-east-africa-company.jpg","cr":{"a":"Sodacan","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Imperial_British_East_Africa_Company.svg"}},"icelandic-commonwealth":{"img":"/images/states/icelandic-commonwealth.jpg","cr":{"a":"Colovia","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Icelandic_Commonwealth_Quarters.svg"}},"islamic-republic-of-afghanistan":{"img":"/images/states/islamic-republic-of-afghanistan.jpg","cr":{"a":"\u0027Fry1989 \u0027","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Afghanistan_(2004%E2%80%932021,_variant).svg"}},"imamate-of-aussa":{"img":"/images/states/imamate-of-aussa.jpg","cr":{"a":"burts","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_flag.svg"}},"iverni":{"t":"People of south-west Ireland named by Ptolemy, whose name is linked to the Érainn and to Ériu, the Irish name for Ireland itself.","o":"Ptolemy\u0027s Geography of about 150 places the Iverni in the south-west of Ireland, around modern Cork, with a town called Ivernis and a river Iernus nearby. Their name is related to Ivernia or Hibernia, the classical name for the island, and to the Érainn, a population group prominent in the early genealogies of Munster.","r":"Classical sources record nothing of their rulers or customs. Early Irish tradition remembers the Érainn as an ancient people of Munster, ancestors of groups such as the Corcu Loigde and the Corcu Duibne, who were powerful before the rise of the Eóganachta. The region has many ogham stones, the earliest Irish writing.","e":"By the early medieval period the Érainn had been eclipsed by the Eóganachta, who built the Kingdom of Munster around Cashel. Érainn descendants such as the Corcu Loigde survived as subordinate kingdoms in west Cork.","re":"Celtic polytheism","la":"Goidelic Celtic","c":"low","img":"/images/states/iverni.jpg","cr":{"a":"NASA","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemy%27s_Ireland.png"}},"itanos":{"img":"/images/states/itanos.jpg","cr":{"a":"Vadim Indeikin","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%92%D0%B8%D0%B4_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8B%D1%80%D1%8C_%D1%81%D0%BE_%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%8F%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8._Toplou._Lasithi._Crete._Greece._%D0%90%D0%B2%D0%B3%D1%83%D1%81%D1%82_2013_-_panoramio.jpg"}},"illinois-confederation":{"img":"/images/states/illinois-confederation.jpg","cr":{"a":"General Georges-Henri-Victor Collot","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaskaskia_Illinois.jpg"}},"itza-kingdom-of-nojpeten":{"img":"/images/states/itza-kingdom-of-nojpeten.jpg","cr":{"a":"Itza Kingdom.jpg: Mabarlabin Maya civilization location map-blank.svg: Sémhur derivative work: rowanwindwhistler (talk)","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Itza_Kingdom.svg"}},"illyrian-provinces":{"img":"/images/states/illyrian-provinces.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg"}},"italian-regency-of-carnaro":{"img":"/images/states/italian-regency-of-carnaro.jpg","cr":{"a":"No machine-readable author provided. Decius assumed (based on copyright claims).","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Free_State_of_Fiume_1920-1924.png"}},"iacetani":{"t":"A Pyrenean people of the Jaca valley in Aragon, whose town Iaca is the ancestor of modern Jaca.","o":"The Iacetani lived in the upper valley of the Aragón river in the central Pyrenees, around modern Jaca, from at least the 5th century BCE. Their affiliation is uncertain: they may have been related to the Vascones or to the Iberian peoples to the south.","r":"Strabo places them in the foothills of the Pyrenees, and their town Iaca later minted coins with an Iberian legend. They lived from herding and farming in the mountain valleys. Nothing reliable is known of their rulers or institutions.","e":"They appear among the peoples subdued during Cato\u0027s campaign of 195 BCE, though the reference is disputed. Later they lay within Hispania Citerior, and during the Sertorian war their region was fought over; Iaca survived as a Roman town and gave its name to Jaca.","c":"low"},"islamic-republic-of-iran":{"img":"/images/states/islamic-republic-of-iran.jpg","cr":{"a":"SVG file: SiBr4Designer: Hamid NadimiConstruction: ISIRI","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Iran_(official).svg"}},"idrisid-emirate-of-asir":{"img":"/images/states/idrisid-emirate-of-asir.jpg","cr":{"a":"Abo Yemen","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Emirate_of_Asir.svg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-werden":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-werden.jpg","cr":{"a":"","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Essen_Kloster_Werden_Innenhof_2_2005.jpg"}},"independent-state-of-croatia":{"img":"/images/states/independent-state-of-croatia.jpg","cr":{"a":"public domain by User:Zscout370","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Croatia_(1941%E2%80%931945).svg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-zwiefalten":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-zwiefalten.jpg","cr":{"a":"Franz Joseph Spiegler / Johann Michael Feuchtmayer","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zwiefalten_Muenster.jpg"}},"idar-state":{"img":"/images/states/idar-state.jpg","cr":{"a":"Rudolf Swoboda","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Pratap_Singh.jpg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-lorsch":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-lorsch.jpg","cr":{"a":"Kuebi - Armin Kübelbeck","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kloster_Lorsch_06.jpg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-saint-maximin":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-saint-maximin.jpg","cr":{"a":"Unknown authorUnknown author","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St._Maximin_(Stich).gif"}},"iceni":{"t":"East Anglian kingdom whose queen Boudica led the great revolt of 60 or 61, burning Camulodunum, Londinium and Verulamium before Rome crushed the rising.","o":"The Iceni held Norfolk and parts of Suffolk and Cambridgeshire; they are probably the Cenimagni who surrendered to Julius Caesar in 54 BCE. In the 1st century BCE their elite deposited spectacular gold torcs at Snettisham, and from about 10 BCE they issued silver coins, some inscribed ECEN, with horse designs.","r":"Coins name rulers such as Antedios, and settlements like Thetford and Saham Toney appear to have been major centres. After the Roman conquest of 43 the Iceni became a client kingdom, but they rebelled in 47 when the governor Ostorius Scapula tried to disarm them. Prasutagus later ruled as a client king, enjoying Roman favour while keeping horse-rearing and an independent elite.","e":"When Prasutagus died around 60, leaving half his realm to Nero, Roman officials seized it, flogged his widow Boudica and raped her daughters. Boudica led the Iceni and Trinovantes in revolt and destroyed three cities before Suetonius Paulinus defeated her. The territory was annexed and later organised as a civitas centred on Venta Icenorum.","ru":["Antedios","Prasutagus","Boudica"],"re":"Celtic polytheism","la":"Common Brittonic","img":"/images/states/iceni.jpg","cr":{"a":"England_Celtic_tribes_-_South.png: Original uploader was Yorkshirian athttp://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title...","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Territory_of_the_Iceni.svg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-prum":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-prum.jpg","cr":{"a":"Heiliges_Römisches_Reich_1400.png: Gustav Droysen derivative work: OwenBlacker","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reichksabtei_Pr%C3%BCm.png"}},"imperial-abbey-of-saint-emmeram":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-saint-emmeram.jpg","cr":{"a":"Dr. Bernd Gross","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0 de","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schloss_St._Emmeram_Regensburg_32.JPG"}},"italiote-league":{"img":"/images/states/italiote-league.jpg","cr":{"a":"Future Perfect at Sunrise","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magna_Graecia_ancient_colonies_and_dialects-eu.svg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-herford":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-herford.jpg","cr":{"a":"\"Ingo Kirschnereit Cyclejakob\"","l":"CC BY 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muensterkirche-frontview.jpg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-lindau":{"img":"/images/states/imperial-abbey-of-lindau.jpg","cr":{"a":"Matthias Zirngibl from Germany","l":"CC BY 2.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lindau_Stiftskirche_und_St_Stephan.jpg"}},"imperial-abbey-of-